B08d8 — isolated numerical dependency repair, 2026-09-28 local time
================================================================

This is the user-approved PATCHED musl 1.2.6 supplement, not a replacement for
the frozen original rung. No installed source/object/archive or original FAIL
receipt was changed. Explicit replacement objects precede each original archive
on the linker command line; all 192 final maps verify both replacements and no
old floatscan/powf archive member. The same preserved five-second/100-KiB-stack
libc-test supervisor executes every case.

Three source defects repaired in two objects:

1. hexfloat's collected digit count must round LDBL_MANT_DIG/4 upward. This
   backports the arithmetic change from musl upstream commit
   50979c5bc89a7b02023e5c0a5ea1ca4da8616a91 (Rich Felker, 2026-05-21):
   https://repo.or.cz/musl.git/commit/50979c5bc89a7b02023e5c0a5ea1ca4da8616a91
   The independently inspected commit describes exactly the two frozen failures.

2. The expanded matrix exposed another hexfloat defect: with fewer than 32
   effective significand bits, bias+x+y may round both additions upward. For
   example 0x8.1111111111111111111111111110000p-16494 in upward mode must round
   to binary128 subnormal bit pattern 9, not 10. Preserve the integer x and a
   nonzero fractional tail as x+0.5, an EXACT <=33-bit value, before adding the
   bias. On this branch the target rounding grid is at least 2 integer units:
   any tail in (0,1) has the same relation to every target value/midpoint as
   0.5. This preserves below/at/above-half classification, including bits=31,
   without the second directed rounding. bits>=32 retains the original path.

3. powf(x,1) for non-NaN x now returns x before approximate log/exp work. This
   preserves both signed zeros, all finite values/subnormals and infinities in
   all rounding modes, without new INEXACT/UNDERFLOW/OVERFLOW. NaNs retain the
   original arithmetic path; no new library NaN sign/payload guarantee is made.

The small fixture's binary128 expected values use only integer significand
quotient/remainder rounding, not host FP, APFloat, strtold or oracle agreement.
5 leading nibbles x 2 patterns x 6 tails x 6 exponents x 2 signs x 4 modes x
2 entry points (strtold, scanf) = 5760 checks. These include ordinary values,
very small subnormals, the 31/32-bit branch boundary and large finite values.
40 powf identity/status checks x 4 modes = 160 checks, including pre-existing
DIVBYZERO, qNaN and sNaN. Total 5920 checks per execution.

Final result:
  GCC14 / Clang19 / EvoCC x O0/O2 x reference/mixed base archives = 12 lanes.
  12/12 focused executions PASS, 71040/71040 checks.
  15 original libc-test entry names x 12 lanes = 180/180 original replays PASS.
  These are eight distinct original source programs; seven retain both ordinary
  and -static entry identities, which share a test object in the frozen build.
  Both configurations link statically, just as the frozen static rung does.
  No shared-loader coverage is inferred from the two entry names.
  Exact combined population: 192/192 completed PASS, no skips/timeouts.
  301 ladder Python tests PASS; Ruff and git diff --check PASS.

Original programs: functional/{strtold,strtof,strtod,strtod_long,strtod_simple,
sscanf,sscanf_long}{,-static} and math/powf. Original assertions/test objects
are unchanged. The two strtold and one powf original failures are now green ONLY
with the patched composition. The original archives still fail those programs.

